---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'About Genshin Damage Calculator — Method & Author';
const description =
  'Who builds the Genshin Damage Calculator, how the five-multiplier damage formula works, where the data comes from, and how often it is refreshed.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="page-shell section-pad">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-forest-600">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)] md:text-5xl">
      An independent, transparent damage calculator for Genshin Impact
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-[65ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
      Genshin Damage Calculator is a free, fan-made theorycrafting tool that computes exact damage numbers for every
      playable character using the official five-multiplier formula. It is built and maintained by Kai Ren, a
      long-time Genshin Impact player, and requires no signup or download.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)]">Who is behind this tool?</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
      The calculator is written and maintained by Kai Ren, who has played Genshin Impact since version 1.0 and
      theorycrafts team rotations as a hobby. Every preset in the roster — character stats, weapons, artifacts, and
      buff assumptions — is hand-checked against the live game within 48 hours of each version patch. You can read
      the full changelog on the <a href="/" class="text-forest-600 underline underline-offset-4">homepage under
      “Data &amp; updates”</a> or reach out via the <a href="/contact/"
      class="text-forest-600 underline underline-offset-4">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)]">How are damage numbers calculated?</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
      The engine multiplies five independent factors from the official in-game formula: Total ATK × Skill Multiplier ×
      (1 + DMG Bonus) × CRIT × Reaction, then applies enemy DEF and RES. Amplifying reactions use the official
      Vaporize (×1.5) and Melt (×2.0) coefficients with the standard Elemental Mastery scaling of
      2.78 × EM ÷ (EM + 1400). Transformative reactions ignore ATK and CRIT and scale with character level and EM.
      The full breakdown is documented in the <a href="/#formula"
      class="text-forest-600 underline underline-offset-4">damage formula section</a> on the homepage.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)]">Where does the data come from?</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
      Character base stats, weapon stats, and talent multipliers are transcribed from the live game and cross-checked
      against HoYoverse’s official announcements.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--text)]">Independence &amp; affiliation</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[65ch] leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
      This is an independent fan-made project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by HoYoverse,
      miHoYo, or Cognosphere. Genshin Impact and all related names, characters, and assets are property of their
      respective owners. The tool is free, shows no paywall, and never asks for account credentials. See our
      <a href="/privacy/" class="text-forest-600 underline underline-offset-4">privacy policy</a> and
      <a href="/terms/" class="text-forest-600 underline underline-offset-4">terms of use</a> for details.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
